# Wall guard. Reacts to the captain's death, the tags, the new captain.
%rec: OpeningBranch

cond: HasFlag('a_new_captain')
goto: NewCaptain

cond: HasFlag('Killed(gate_captain)')
goto: CaptainDead

cond: true
goto: Default

%rec: Nodes

name: Default
npc: Yard's closed. Talk to the captain if you want the airlock.
#
o_text: Who are the people out there?
o_id: ines_bodies
o_goto: Bodies
#
o_text: What's on the terminals?
o_id: ines_terminals
o_goto: Terminals
#
o_text: Never mind.
o_id: ines_bye
o_goto: Bye

name: Bodies
npc: The south gate four hundred. Terra Vitae people, mostly. They wanted in when the dome sealed. Orders came down. (She keeps her eyes on the field.) I was on the other gate that night. That is what I tell myself.
#
o_text: Somebody is looking for one of them. Burton.
o_id: ines_burton
o_cond: HasFlag('JobAccepted(tags)') && !HasItem('burton_dog_tag')
o_goto: Burton
#
o_text: Back.
o_id: ines_bodies_back
o_goto: Default

name: Burton
npc: Young one, by the east pylon, with a chain at his neck. Nobody took it. Nobody goes out there. (Quieter.) If you bring it back to his people, I didn't help.
effect: SetFlag('ines_pointed_burton')
#
o_text: Thanks.
o_id: ines_burton_back
o_goto: Default

name: Terminals
npc: Gate log copies and the yard camera. The captain keeps the log on him, the terminals just echo it. Nobody reads them.
#
o_text: Back.
o_id: ines_terminals_back
o_goto: Default

name: CaptainDead
npc: (Her hand is on her pistol.) They found him in the yard. If it was you, walk away now and don't come back for a while.
#
o_text: I'm going.
o_id: ines_dead_bye
o_goto: Bye

name: NewCaptain
npc: New captain, new rules. Fifty a visit to the yard. He keeps it, of course.
#
o_text: Of course.
o_id: ines_new_bye
o_goto: Bye

name: Bye
npc: Move along.
effect: EndConversation
